# SQLmap

SQLmap is an automated tool for detecting and exploiting SQL injection vulnerabilities.

It supports multiple database management systems and can automate SQL injection testing, database enumeration, and data extraction.

Personal notes and reference for using SQLmap in cybersecurity labs and CTFs.

---

# Basic Syntax

```bash
sqlmap [options]
```

---

# Target

| Option | Description |
|---|---|
| `-u <URL>` | Target URL |
| `--data=<DATA>` | POST data |
| `-r <FILE>` | Load HTTP request from file |
| `-l <FILE>` | Parse targets from Burp/Web logs |
| `-m <FILE>` | Scan multiple targets |
| `-g <DORK>` | Process Google dork results |
| `--url` | Target URL |

---

# URL Parameters

SQLmap commonly tests parameters included in the target request.

For example:

```text
?id=FUZZ
```

A specific parameter can be marked for testing with:

```text
*
```

This is useful when a request contains several parameters and only one should be tested.

---

# Detection

| Option | Description |
|---|---|
| `--level=<1-5>` | Level of tests performed |
| `--risk=<1-3>` | Risk level of tests |
| `--technique=<BEUSTQ>` | Specify SQL injection techniques |
| `--dbms=<DBMS>` | Specify database management system |
| `--batch` | Use default answers automatically |

Higher `--level` values test more parameters and payloads.

Higher `--risk` values can use more aggressive tests.

---

# SQL Injection Techniques

| Code | Technique |
|---|---|
| `B` | Boolean-based blind |
| `E` | Error-based |
| `U` | UNION query-based |
| `S` | Stacked queries |
| `T` | Time-based blind |
| `Q` | Inline queries |

Specify techniques with:

```text
--technique=BEUSTQ
```

